This section embeds the final algorithm as runnable JavaScript snippets. The implementation mirrors the TypeScript module in `code/src/proof/modularInverse.ts`:
- GCD pre-check to ensure an inverse can exist
- Multiplier choice `k = ceil(y / r)` with small positive offsets to avoid traps
- Depth-first bounded backtracking to enforce decreasing remainders
- Optional fallback to the Extended Euclidean method for completeness

